  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Getting new countertops is a game-changer for your kitchen, but knowing what to expect can make the process super smooth. First, your base cabinets absolutely need to be fully installed, level, and secure before anyone even thinks about templating. Any adjustments to the cabinets should be done beforehand! Then, a professional will come to create a template, either with physical patterns or fancy digital laser measurements. This captures your exact cabinet layout, wall contours, and spots for your sink and cooktop. After templating, there’s usually a bit of a wait — often 1 to 3 weeks — while your countertops are fabricated off-site. This is where they're cut, polished, and have all the edge profiles and cutouts done. When installation day arrives, they'll dry-fit the countertops first, then secure them to your cabinets with adhesives or fasteners, ensuring everything is perfectly level. Seams, if you have them, will be joined with color-matched epoxy. Lastly, any required sealing for stone materials will be done, and backsplashes will be cut and fitted. Don't forget that plumbing and gas hookups usually happen *after* the countertop is installed. If you have questions about your specific project, give HH Remodeling LLC a call. We're here to help Denver-area homeowners."
    }
  ],
